      "prompt": "Solve 5^(x+3) = 625^(2x).",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Write both sides as powers of 5: 5 = 5^1 and 625 = 5^4",
        "5^(x+3) = 625^(2x) becomes 5^(x+3) = 5^(4×2x), i.e. 5^(x+3) = 5^(8x)",
        "Since the bases match, the powers must be equal: x + 3 = 8x",
        "Rearranging: -7x = -3, so x = -3/-7 = 3/7"
      ],
      "final_answer": "3/7",
      "marks": 5,
