      "topic_id": "rationalise_denominator",
      "prompt": "Rationalise the denominator of 10/(9 - √14), giving your answer in its simplest form.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, (9 + √14):",
        "10/(9 - √14) = 10(9 + √14) / [(9 - √14)(9 + √14)]",
        "The denominator is a difference of two squares: 9^2 - 14 = 67",
        "The numerator is 10(9 + √14) = 90 + 10√14",
        "= (90 + 10√14)/67"
      ],
      "final_answer": "(90 + 10√14)/67",
